---
// The Findish wordmark: the name in Atkinson bold, with "dish" sitting in a shallow nori
// bowl, so it reads as find + dish (a curved stroke that grows out of the d, Kyle's pick, 2026-11-16). Pure text and CSS: it scales with the font size it's
// given, follows light and dark mode, and screen readers hear one word, "Findish".
---

<span class="wordmark">Fin<span class="wordmark-dish">dish</span></span>

<style>
  .wordmark {
    display: inline-block;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .wordmark-dish {
    position: relative;
    display: inline-block;
    padding-inline: 0.02em 0.04em;
  }

  /* The bowl: a curved stroke under "dish" that starts out of the d's round, so the d
     reads as the connector between "find" and "dish". Decoration only. */
  .wordmark-dish::after {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    inset-inline: -0.06em -0.02em;
    bottom: -0.1em;
    height: 0.26em;
    border: 0.085em solid var(--accent-ink);
    border-top: 0;
    border-radius: 0 0 50% 50% / 0 0 100% 100%;
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  @media (forced-colors: active) {
    .wordmark-dish::after {
      border-color: CanvasText;
    }
  }
</style>
